  "generated_text": ".. Rearrange the equation to set it equal to zero:\n\\[56x^2 + 27 - 89x + 8 = 0\\]\n\\[56x^2 - 89x + 35 = 0\\]\n\n2. Factor the quadratic equation:\n\\[56x^2 - 89x + 35 = (7x - 5)(8x - 7)\\]\n\n3. Solve for $x$ by setting each factor equal to zero:\n\\[7x - 5 = 0 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{5}{7}\\]\n\\[8x - 7 = 0 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{7}{8}\\]\n\n4. Identify the other solution:\nThe other solution $ $x = \\frac{7}{8}$.\n\nConclusion:\nThe other value of $x$ that solves the equation is $\\boxed{\\frac{7}{8}}$.",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[7/8, '\\\\frac{7}{8}']",
    "gold_answer": "First of all, let us place everything to one side: \\begin{align*}\n56x^2 + 27 &= 89x - 8\\\\\n56x^2 - 89x + 35 &= 0.\n\\end{align*}Now we must factor. Knowing that $x = \\frac{5}{7}$ is a solution to this equation, we can reason that $(7x - 5)$ must be one of the factors of $56x^2 - 89x + 35$ which means that $(8x - 7)$ must be the other factor, since the linear terms must multiply to $56x^2$ and the constant terms must multiply to $35.$\n\nWe can easily verify that indeed, $56x^2 - 89x + 35 = (7x - 5)(8x - 7),$ therefore $x = \\boxed{\\frac{7}{8}}$ is our answer.",
    "is_correct": true
  },
